    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You are given a binary string <var>S</var> made of <const>0</const>s and <const>1</const>s.<br><br>Generate every possible subsequence of <var>S</var> by picking any subset of characters while keeping their relative order. <br><br>Treat each subsequence as a binary number and convert it to an integer (an empty subsequence counts as <const>0</const>).<br><br>Compute the total bitwise XOR sum of all these integer values.<br><br>Reference on what bitwise XOR is: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation<br><br><strong>Example:</strong><br><var>S</var> = &quot;<const>101</const>&quot;<br>Subsequences: &quot;&quot;, &quot;<const>1</const>&quot;, &quot;<const>0</const>&quot;, &quot;<const>1</const>&quot;, &quot;<const>10</const>&quot;, &quot;<const>11</const>&quot;, &quot;<const>01</const>&quot;, &quot;<const>101</const>&quot;<br>Integer values: <const>0</const>, <const>1</const>, <const>0</const>, <const>1</const>, <const>2</const>, <const>3</const>, <const>1</const>, <const>5</const><br>Bitwise XOR total: <const>0</const> XOR <const>1</const> XOR <const>0</const> XOR <const>1</const> XOR <const>2</const> XOR <const>3</const> XOR <const>1</const> XOR <const>5</const> = <const>5</const></span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> <var>N</var>, an integer, denoting the length of the binary string <var>S</var><br><strong>Line 2:</strong> <var>S</var>, a single binary string of length <var>N</var>, consisting solely of the characters <const>0</const> and <const>1</const>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> <var>X</var>, denoting the total bitwise XOR sum of the base-<const>2</const> values of all subsequences of <var>S</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\"><const>1</const> &lt;= <var>N</var> &lt;= <const>50</const></div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">3\n101</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-out\">5</pre>\n         </div>\n      </div>\n   </div>\n</div>"
